# OBSX Security Dual-License Structure

Copyright (c) 2026 Alexis Grimmace (https://obsx.tech)

OBSX Security uses a **Dual-License Structure** with clear file-level boundaries:

- **Zone 1 (`MIT`)**: Core Protocol Engine, Client SDK, Verification Middleware, TypeScript Definitions, Build Tooling, Tests, Package Manifests, and Public Documentation (`lib/core.js`, `lib/crypto.js`, `lib/telemetry.js`, `lib/kv.js`, `lib/config.js`, `lib/index.js`, `index.d.ts`, `package.json`, `.gitignore`, `src/tracer.js`, compiled client bundles, `public/index.html`, `public/docs.html`, `public/notes.html`, `public/notes.js`, `public/app.js`, `public/style.css`, `public/privacy.html`, `public/terms.html`, `public/install.md`, public static icons/diagrams in `public/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `README.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `docs/` including `docs/README.baseline.md`).
- **Zone 2 (`LicenseRef-OBSX-Zone-2-1.0` — OBSX Source-Available License v1.0)**: Self-Hosted Operator Server, Origin Shield, Auto-Updater, Account & Mailer Subsystems, Operator Dashboard UI, and Deployment/Load-Testing Tooling (`server.js`, `lib/botshield.js`, `lib/updater.js`, `lib/accounts.js`, `lib/mailer.js`, `public/dashboard.html`, `public/dashboard.js`, `tools/flood.js`, `.env.example`, `.github/`).
- **Closed-Source / Proprietary Modules (Excluded — No License Granted)**: Proprietary operational modules maintained outside this public repository (`OBSX Sentinel™` proprietary engine and closed-source edge infrastructure) are strictly proprietary, excluded from distribution and npm `"files"` allowlists, and receive no license grant under this file.

**Prospective Applicability**: This Dual-License Structure governs releases from **v2.2.0 onward**. Historical commits and releases published strictly prior to v2.2.0 under the MIT License remain licensed under MIT for those prior versions. Any future license updates apply prospectively to future versions only and do not retroactively revoke rights already validly granted for prior versions.

**Precedence & Severability**: Standalone use of Zone 1 files is governed exclusively by the MIT License in Part 1 without additional restriction. Use of Zone 2 files (or combined server deployments incorporating Zone 2 components) is governed by Part 2 with respect to Zone 2 software components. If any provision of this license is held unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue in full force and effect.

**Contributor License Agreement (CLA)**: By submitting a pull request or contribution to this repository, you agree that your contribution is licensed under the Part governing the file(s) you modify or add (Part 1 MIT for Zone 1; Part 2 OBSX Source-Available License v1.0 for Zone 2).

